## Task: `W062-GFORM-R03-SCOPE-SAFE-RULE-CANDIDATE-01`
Pre-registered (before first run) 4-tool × 11-target matrix, 2 deterministic runs/cell, 7 pinned inputs, 8 controls. Built **E4**, a one-hunk scope-aware replacement of the R03 binder block: a non-literal composite binder passes only when located quantifier phrases align 1:1 with declared binders by count and kind, and every binder variable sits inside that quantifier's **own restriction phrase**. Sandbox-only; no canonical/instrument byte written.

**Result (all cells matched pre-registration, E13 PASS):**

| | baseline | E3 | **E4** |
|---|---|---|---|
| frozen F1 (variable-wise) | reject/R03 | accept | **accept** |
| scope error (lead's V3) | reject/R03 | **accept** | **reject/R03** |
| unbound-restriction / shadow-quantifier | reject | **accept** | **reject** |
| grouped, product, reordered | accept/reject | accept | **accept** |
| F2a/F2b canonical | accept | accept | **accept** |

So E4 is the first measured A-prime candidate: fixes the false positive without cand_E3's over-acceptance. The lead's E3 finding independently reproduced at `3f69bc1eb27a`. Direct runs on the published canonical bytes corroborate (`doc_sha256 = d9cebb9404b2`).

